# Recommended / declared scope shown to the user in the LSPosed manager.
#
# One package name per line. Use `system` (NOT `android`) for system_server —
# that is the modern-API vocabulary. Legacy modules use the inverted convention
# and the framework silently swaps the two, which is the classic scope bug when
# porting an old module.
#
# A recommended scope is only a hint: the manager lets the user pick which of
# these are actually active, and RegTrail also requests scope at runtime through
# XposedService.requestScope() (see the app's "目标" screen).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `system` is REQUIRED.
#
# The permission-free floating window works by hooking
# PhoneWindowManager.checkAddPermission, and PhoneWindowManager only exists
# inside system_server. Without `system` in scope, RegTrail cannot neutralise
# the SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW requirement, and adding an overlay window from a
# target app will be rejected with a SecurityException.
#
# Target apps are NOT listed here on purpose: RegTrail is a general-purpose
# tool, so which apps to inject into is the user's choice, not a fixed set. Pick
# them in the LSPosed manager, or press "申请已勾选" on the app's 目标 screen and
# approve the framework's prompt.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
system
